A NOTE ON WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT DO, because pretending otherwise would be
dishonest:

Claude Code has no licence enforcement, no entitlement checking and no billing.
The `license` field in a plugin manifest is a string nobody reads. This document
is therefore a statement of terms — the thing a reviewer or a legal team looks
for — and it is not a control.

The actual control is the API token. Every call this plugin's MCP server makes is
validated server-side against your account. That is where access is granted and
revoked, and it is the only place it could meaningfully live, because everything
in this directory is on your disk and readable by you.

Questions: https://plexarm.com
